  "caption": "Quinn sat through a three-movie marathon, then met the stairs. Cue an ache right around the kneecap.\n\nPain around or behind the kneecap on stairs, squats or long sitting is often about load: the knee has been asked to do more than it's currently ready for. The kneecap usually isn't \"out of place\", and clicks alone aren't damage.\n\nWhat often helps: trimming the load for a while (shallower squats, fewer hills, splitting up stair-heavy tasks), building quad and hip strength, and progressing depth, reps and speed gradually. Taping can help some people short term, and squats don't need to be banned forever.\n\nGet it checked after a big knock, or with large swelling, locking, repeated giving way, fever, or pain that keeps worsening.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
